  "description": "Faithfully extracted from KernelGenBench cuBLAS test_cublasCgemvStridedBatched.py. Strided-batched complex64 GEMV y = alpha*op(A)*x + beta*y over real 3D tensors (batchCount,M,N). trans fixed to int 0 ('N') as the test passes to the baseline, so lenx=N, leny=M; lda=A.shape[1]=M, strideA=M*N, stridex=N, stridey=M. alpha/beta are complex in the op but only purely-real combos from the test's list are used here (represented as float scalars, imag=0), noted for faithfulness. _random_tensor does not support complex, so A/x/y are built by gen_inputs as complex64. reference mutates y in place and returns it. Uses real 3D tensors (not device-pointer arrays), so it is data-driven-safe. Requires kernelgenbench + cuBLAS at eval time.",
